--- !u!1001 &8181327551074553223
PrefabInstance:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  serializedVersion: 2
  m_Modification:
    serializedVersion: 3
    m_TransformParent: {fileID: 2789392890698996192}
    m_Modifications:
    - target: {fileID: 2116517601969916342, guid: 183e809bca3827e41a67b7345a91f0c2, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: Augmented reality attempts to merge both reality and digital information
        into one medium. In the case of video games, real world locations or gyroscopic
        controls with cameras were commonly used for the AR Notable titles such as
        Pokemon GO, Face Raiders and Ingress combined AR with video game to encourage
        players to interact with the world in real time through activities in-game.
        Interactions in the real world brought players to engage with each other
        socially through the game; Pokemon GO was able to shift culture through its
        global success. However, their success was greatly hindered by the COVID-19
        pandemic, causing many live service AR games to shut down or face severe
        loss in an attempt to compensate for the lockdowns.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 2116517601969916342, guid: 183e809bca3827e41a67b7345a91f0c2, type: 3}
